# Build context allowlist.
#
# Without this file `docker build .` tars and ships the entire repository to
# the daemon before the first instruction runs. That is 34 GB here, almost all
# of it result tables, genotype files and cached single-cell objects that no
# Dockerfile copies. The two Dockerfiles between them need about 880 KB.
#
# The analysis data is not baked into the image on purpose: it is bind-mounted
# at run time, so the image stays small and the tables it reads are the ones on
# the host, which is what makes the acceptance run a comparison rather than a
# replay of something frozen inside the image.

# Exclude everything, then allow back only what a COPY line names.
*

!container/
!cqtna_r/
!150a_environment.lock

# ...but never these, even inside the allowed directories.
cqtna_r/**/*.Rcheck
cqtna_r/**/*.tar.gz
**/.Rhistory
**/.RData
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
